---
import InfoLayout from '../layouts/InfoLayout.astro';
import { SITE_CONFIG } from '../config/site';

const name = SITE_CONFIG.name;
---

<InfoLayout
  title="Terms of Use"
  description={`The terms for using ${name}: free in-browser image tools, provided as is. You keep every right to your images.`}
  path="terms"
  updated="Last updated 25 October 2026"
>
  <p>
    These terms apply when you use {name} (the "site"), run by {SITE_CONFIG.operator} in {SITE_CONFIG.operatorCountry}. By using the
    site you agree to them. If you don't agree, please don't use the site.
  </p>

  <h2>The service</h2>
  <p>
    The site offers free image tools that run in your web browser. You don't need an account. Tools may be added, changed or removed at
    any time, and the site may be unavailable from time to time.
  </p>

  <h2>Your images and content</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You keep all rights to the images you open and the files you create. We don't receive them and claim no rights to them.</li>
    <li>
      Only edit images you have the right to use, and don't use the site for anything illegal, to infringe other people's rights, or to
      create content that harasses, deceives or harms others.
    </li>
    <li>You are responsible for how you use the files you create.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Check results before you rely on them</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>AI background removal, compression and conversion results vary from image to image. Check every result before you use it.</li>
    <li>
      Blur and pixelation can sometimes be partly reversed on small text. To hide sensitive information such as ID numbers, use the
      solid black bar in the censor tool.
    </li>
    <li>
      For photos and documents with official requirements (passports, applications, exams), check the requirements of the organization
      you are submitting to. The presets on this site are a starting point, not a guarantee of acceptance.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Open source</h2>
  <p>
    The site's code is free software under the GNU Affero General Public License v3.0 (AGPL-3.0), and the
    <a href={SITE_CONFIG.sourceUrl} rel="noopener">source code is public</a>. It includes third-party components under their own
    licenses, which are listed in the source code. These terms do not limit your rights under those licenses.
  </p>

  <h2>No warranty</h2>
  <p>
    The site is provided "as is" and "as available", without warranties of any kind, express or implied, including fitness for a
    particular purpose and non-infringement.
  </p>

  <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the fullest extent permitted by law, {SITE_CONFIG.operator} is not liable for any indirect, incidental or consequential loss, or
    for any loss of data or files, arising from your use of the site. Keep a copy of your original images.
  </p>

  <h2>Governing law</h2>
  <p>These terms are governed by the laws of India.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>If these terms change, the new version will be posted here with a new date. Using the site after a change means you accept it.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about these terms: <a href={`mailto:${SITE_CONFIG.contactEmail}`}>{SITE_CONFIG.contactEmail}</a>.
  </p>
</InfoLayout>
